# Reductions for exclusion of the small-component alternative

The checked reductions construct the comparison L/O₂(L) ≃ L* after
simplicity is known, derive the elementary abelian and Frattini properties
of D⁺ in the centralizing branch, and reduce conjugate generation in the
abelian cases to the actual irreducible intersections.

`SourceData.markedMS` now constructs the marked V₂-line, genuine MS-pair,
surviving module alternatives and quotient comparison from the authorized
universal earlier classifications and genuine earlier local conclusions.
The source setup also places V₂ in the actual Z(Q), identifies its relative
normalizer with M ∩ L and proves the required O^{3′} residual identity.

The central-cover calculation is checked for every marked coefficient
configuration, including L₃(2), which is absent from I.2.3. ModelTransport
transfers all three linear cases to whole-core or whole-center coordinates,
preserving the quotient actor and both dual summands in case (3).

The small-alternative source exclusion now constructs all five marked models
from the original MS conclusion and proves their core-centralization inputs.
The natural cases use the full literal star centralizer and actual ambient
irreducible summands. `SourceWitnesses.excluded_of_classifications` applies
the unchanged earlier MS/FF classifications to the original source setup
and small-parabolic marking; these earlier source inputs still need discharge.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
printed pp.1131–1132 (PDF pp.1148–1149), 15.3.28–31.
-/
